# Wise incoming payments integration
SLYCUSTOM_TAB_WISE=Wise
WISE_STATUS_SECTION=Wise integration status
SLYCUSTOM_WISE_SECTION=Wise connection and matching
WISE_WEBHOOK_URL=Webhook receiver URL
WISE_API_TOKEN=Wise API token
WISE_API_TOKENTooltip=Token created in Wise Settings > Developer tools > API tokens. Stored per company/entity. Used to pull balance statements (payment references) and, later, to create transfers.
WISE_PROFILE_ID=Wise profile id
WISE_PROFILE_IDTooltip=Numeric id of the Wise profile. Auto-filled by the "Test connection" button when the token is valid.
WISE_SIGNATURE_KEY=Webhook signature key
WISE_SIGNATURE_KEY_FOUND=Verification enabled (verification_key.pem found)
WISE_SIGNATURE_KEY_MISSING=Bootstrap mode: save the subscription public key to DOL_DATA_ROOT/wise_webhook/verification_key.pem to enforce signature verification (unsigned deliveries are currently accepted with a warning)
WISE_QUEUE_STATUS=Incoming payments queue
WISE_SO_REF_PATTERN=SO reference extraction pattern
WISE_SO_REF_PATTERNTooltip=Optional manual override. Effective pattern resolution: this field > derived from the order numbering mask (Sales Orders setup > Orders numbering, e.g. COMMANDE_SAPHIR_MASK) > built-in default. Leave empty to stay automatic.
WISE_PAYMENT_MODE=Payment mode
WISE_PAYMENT_MODETooltip=Dolibarr payment mode recorded on payments created from Wise credits (default VIR = bank transfer).
WISE_BANK_ACCOUNT_DEFAULT=Default bank account
WISE_BANK_ACCOUNT_DEFAULTTooltip=Bank account used for the payment bank line when no per-currency mapping matches.
WISE_BANK_MAPPING_CUR=%s bank account
WISE_BANK_MAPPING_CURTooltip=Dolibarr bank account that mirrors the Wise %s balance; recorded credits are written to this account.
WISE_TEST_CONNECTION=Test connection
WISE_TEST_OK=Connection OK. Profiles:
WISE_TEST_KO=Connection failed.
WISE_TOKEN_NOT_SET=No Wise API token configured.
WISE_SO_REF_PATTERN_EFFECTIVE=Effective SO extraction pattern
WISE_SO_REF_SOURCE_MANUAL=Source: manual override
WISE_SO_REF_SOURCE_MASK=Source: derived from order numbering mask
WISE_SO_REF_SOURCE_DEFAULT=Source: built-in default (no mask found)
WISE_SAVE_SIGNATURE_KEY=Fetch and save signature key
WISE_SIGNATURE_KEY_SAVED=Signature key saved. Webhook verification is now enforced.
WISE_SIGNATURE_KEY_NOT_FOUND=No signature key found in the subscriptions response.
WISE_SIGNATURE_KEY_WRITE_FAILED=Could not write the signature key file:
WISE_FLOW_STATUS=Flow status
WISE_FLOW_STATUSTooltip=Incoming: queue Wise credits into the reconcile list. Outgoing: prepare Wise transfers from supplier invoices (await manual funding in Wise).
WISE_FLOW_INCOMING=Incoming (webhook reconciliation)
WISE_FLOW_OUTGOING=Outgoing (API payment preparation)
WISE_INCOMING_ENABLED=Enable incoming payments
WISE_INCOMING_ENABLEDTooltip=When ON, balances#credit webhook deliveries are queued into the reconcile list (NEW status) for enrichment and manual confirmation. The raw events are still stored when OFF.
WISE_OUTGOING_ENABLED=Enable outgoing payment preparation
WISE_OUTGOING_ENABLEDTooltip=When ON, supplier invoices expose Wise transfer preparation (draft transfer created via API, funded manually in the Wise dashboard). Requires the transfers#state-change subscription for automatic status write-back.
SLYCUSTOM_TAB_SHIPSGO=ShipsGo
SLYCUSTOM_SHIPSGO_SECTION=ShipsGo connection
WISE_WEBHOOK_IPCHECK=Webhook source IP allowlist
WISE_WEBHOOK_IPCHECKTooltip=Reject webhook deliveries whose source IP is outside the Wise egress networks (45.129.54.0/24, 45.129.55.0/24 per docs.wise.com). Interim hardening while the signature public key is not available; combines with signature verification when both are on.
WISE_IPCHECK_ACTIVE=Source IP allowlist active (interim protection).
WISE_SIGNATURE_KEYTooltip=The subscription public key Wise generates automatically. Look for it on the subscription detail page in Wise Settings > Developer tools > Webhooks, then save it to DOL_DATA_ROOT/wise_webhook/verification_key.pem (or use the fetch button when the subscriptions API is reachable).

